// Code-signing identity for the macOS app.
//
// **Do not copy this file and edit it. Run README.md's "Signing the macOS
// build" step 3 instead** — one command that writes the finished
// `Signing.xcconfig` with your Team ID already substituted, and there is
// nothing to hand-edit afterwards.
//
// This file stays as documentation of what those settings are and why. It is
// **not** the procedure, and saying it was is a live instance of the exact
// defect task 11.38 was reported for: "copy the template, then edit the Team
// ID" is how somebody comes to paste the wrong ten-character string, and the
// only symptom arrives much later as `No Account for Team "..."`, which reads
// like a missing Apple ID account. Task 11.37's sweep found this file still
// saying it, in the one place the README believed it had closed.
//
// **Why this file exists, and why it is not simply committed with a value.**
// macOS refuses keychain access to an ad-hoc-signed app. The app stores your
// sign-in session in the keychain, so without a real signing identity,
// signing in fails with keychain error `-34018` ("a required entitlement
// isn't present") *after* the server has already accepted and spent your
// sign-in code. That was task 11.38. A Team ID belongs to one Apple
// Developer account and cannot be shared, so the repository cannot carry one
// for you — `AppInfo.xcconfig` pulls this file in with `#include?`, an
// optional include, so the project still builds without it (ad hoc, no
// keychain, no sign-in).
//
// **Where the Team ID comes from, which Team ID is the wrong one, and the
// Xcode route instead of the command line — all of that is README.md's
// "Signing the macOS build", and none of it is repeated here.**
//
// This file used to carry a second copy of the `security find-certificate`
// pipeline, of the warning that `security find-identity`'s parenthesised value
// is the wrong ten characters, and of the Xcode GUI route — under a heading
// saying it was "for reading rather than for copying". Task 11.52's finding is
// that a copy hedged as not-the-procedure is still a copy: task 11.38 replaced
// the Team ID instruction and **this file kept the superseded one**, in the
// one place the README believed it had closed. Removed by task 11.40; the
// class is guarded by `test/documentation/setup_step_ownership_test.dart`.

// The values below are illustrative. README.md step 3 generates the real file.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development

// Selects `Runner/DebugProfile-Signed.entitlements` and
// `Runner/Release-Signed.entitlements`, which declare `keychain-access-groups`.
// Only valid together with a real DEVELOPMENT_TEAM above: Xcode refuses to
// build those files without a development signing certificate. Keep the two
// together — set both, or neither.
TRITRACK_ENTITLEMENTS_SUFFIX = -Signed
